From 527f5a7327dc7aa1ce899b1fc747283a732a93a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:34:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(motion,app): tighten the axis fit's inlier band to
 the revolve's own noise

The robust axis fit sorted normal lines with the 3 % sagitta band
(0.3 mm on an r10 bar), so facets standing near a meridian plane
without lying in one - a cross hole's mouth ring, its floor's centre
strip - stayed inliers and leaned the line ~0.001 mm, past the lathe
spindle law's 0.0005 mm: a bar with one modelled cross hole was refused.

Once the inliers settle, the band now shrinks to 4x the kept facets'
area-weighted median miss (floor 1e-9 of the radius) and the line is
refitted, repeated while the band keeps shrinking. Every tightened
refit must pass the same backstops and the full judgement on all
facets; one that fails is not taken and the last settled (trusted) fit
stands. An exact revolve meets the tight band everywhere and keeps its
plain fit bit for bit. The spindle law's 0.0005 is unchanged.

Pins: lathe_cross_drill a_bar_with_one_modelled_cross_hole_fits_on_
the_spindle_and_drills_clean (main reads worst 0.00088 mm, refused),
axis_robust a_near_meridian_strip_is_set_aside_by_the_tightened_band
(main 3.3e-4 mm off), a_rectangular_prism_is_still_refused_as_not_
revolved. The punched_bar fixture's half-turn mirror holes (#117
workaround) are dropped; the cross-drill suites stay green without them.

Fixes #116

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
