From cb4c4979f2b528fe0989a3235ef0fcb38da485ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:59:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(motion): tighten the axis fit once, from a noise
 scale, and only on improvement

Review of PR #168. The iterated median-shrink band picked facets by the
sign of their noise on noisy meshes and settled on axes worse than the
plain fit, still trusted; and the set-aside share, read at the tight
band, named noise as features on plain bars.

- The wide band is now max(3 % radius, 5 sigma), sigma the MAD scale of
  every facet's miss about the plain fit: a band inside the noise cut
  its tails one-sidedly (main did this past ~15 um of jitter too).
- The wide trim is taken only when it lowers the clipped residual of
  every facet.
- The tightening runs ONCE: band 5 sigma of the coarse inliers, one
  refit with no re-trim, taken only when it passes every gate and lowers
  the coarse inliers' clipped residual. Declined, the wide fit stands
  trusted.
- outlier_share is read at the wide band.
- Tests move to axis_robust_tests.rs (400-line law).

Pins: a_noisy_shaft_with_a_strip_never_fits_worse_than_plain (32-case
jitter x strip sweep, 0.2-17 um; 1 um + strip: 1.8e-4 vs plain 7.0e-4),
a_noisy_plain_shaft_sets_nothing_aside (jitter 1e-5..1e-2 and an f32
shaft at X1234.5 report 0 set aside).

Refs #116

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
